{
  "timestamp": "2026-07-30T15:49:34Z",
  "title": "Multi-Provider BYOK — connect an OpenAI or Gemini key, not just Anthropic",
  "type": "feature",
  "userRequest": "I want to expand BYOK and AI connection beyond claude API Key to allow bringing a key from OpenAI or Gemini and also see if we can connect directly to subscriptions in a more consumer-friendly way. Start with adding OpenAI key ability and Gemini key ability and plan out all of this.",
  "description": "The AI coach now accepts a bring-your-own key from Anthropic, OpenAI, or Gemini instead of Anthropic only. One paste field recognizes the provider from the key's shape (sk-ant- / sk- / AIza), and an unrecognized shape offers a provider picker rather than rejecting a key that may be perfectly valid. All three can be connected at once with one marked active, switchable by tap; disconnecting the active provider promotes another instead of dropping the user to the offline coach. An existing Anthropic key migrates silently because CoachProvider.anthropic still reads the original coach-anthropic-key Keychain account.\n\nBackend: a new shared router (api/_lib/llm.ts) routes coach, race-import, and race-search to whichever provider the request names, with the IDENTICAL coach system prompt and safety rules — the provider changes which model generates the words, never the coaching. Anthropic goes through the SDK; OpenAI and Gemini over plain fetch so no dependency is added to the serverless bundle. Gemini needed real adaptation: no system role (systemInstruction), assistant maps to model, and additionalProperties must be stripped recursively from the response schema or every structured call 400s. Header compatibility runs both ways (new x-ai-provider/x-ai-key plus the legacy x-anthropic-key) because the app and backend cannot deploy atomically — so the backend must go live before the app build, or an OpenAI/Gemini key would connect in-app and then fail.\n\nAlso extracted CoachProviderRow, CoachKeyField, and the shared SettingsActionRow out of SettingsView (991 -> 912 lines), and added the whole BYOK layer to the glossary, which had never been registered.\n\nKnown open item: the default model IDs for OpenAI and Gemini in api/_lib/llm.ts are unverified guesses. Both are env-overridable (COACH_MODEL_OPENAI / COACH_MODEL_GEMINI), so correcting them is configuration, not a release. See docs/codeyam/ai-connection-options.md for why consumer subscriptions (ChatGPT Plus, Claude Pro, Gemini Advanced) cannot be connected instead, and why Apple Foundation Models is the recommended next step toward a no-key coach.",
